  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Keep signing keys in Azure Key Vault. With this package Abblix JWT and Abblix OIDC Server sign tokens and unwrap encryption keys through the vault, so the private half of a key never enters the application process; only public halves reach the JWKS endpoint, and verification stays local. A key that has to be minted in the process is sealed to a vault key before it is stored. One registration call wires the custodian, and a placement call after it names the keys it holds. Full details: https://github.com/Abblix/Oidc.Server/releases/tag/v2.4",
